  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between alpha-Cedrene epoxide and SNU1 through a series of target interactions. The compound is implicated in targeting RXF 631, which in turn is a target of Phyllofolactones F and (7S,11S)-(+)-12-acetoxysydonic acid, both of which directly interact with SNU1. Additionally, alpha-Cedrene epoxide is also linked to MOVP-3, which targets Excisusin C, which also interacts with SNU1. These pathways collectively indicate that alpha-Cedrene epoxide may influence SNU1 through multiple intermediate targets, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between alpha-Cedrene epoxide and SNU1.",
